yaml/null
description: Nothing — ~, null, or an empty value
- >
  The null value has three spellings — `~`, the literal `null` (`Null` and `NULL` accepted
  too), and NOTHING at all: an empty value after the colon is null, the bare key IS the null.
  A SUPERCLASS of
  [json/null](::language:01-Concretes_2:04-json_code:01-json_scalar:03-json_null), which knows
  the one lowercase literal:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: ~
  b: null
  c:
- *..:..:..:..:04-json_code:01-json_scalar:03-json_null
